// BT-3047 / ADR 0109 amendment: a block-taking class method whose hierarchy
// *does* define its own `foo` (distinct from BT3047Ancestor's) — pins the
// "silently executes the wrong method against the wrong class's live state"
// half of the bug. Before the fix, `self foo` inside a block that
// fixtures/bt3047parent.bt hands to this class would resolve against THIS
// class's `foo` (since it happened to run inside this class's process)
// instead of the block's lexical home (BT3047Ancestor, via BT3047Parent).

Value subclass: BT3047DriverWithFoo

  class foo -> Symbol => #FromDriver

  // BT-3047: the block runs inside THIS class's own gen_server process
  // (ADR 0109), not the caller's.
  class run: aBlock :: Block over: aList :: List -> Nil =>
    aList do: [:x | aBlock value: x]
    nil
